A||||7||Homicidal||Strange rattle coming from Rear Right Tire, is the shock going bad?!||||11||
Z||000000||Homicidal||05-01-2001||07:27 PM||||Whenever I hit a rather quick bump, I get a rattling sound, similiar to a peice of somwhat loose metal hitting another peice of stationary metal (rapid clinking).  <P>It used to be less noticable, but I think it's getting more and more apparent, which can only mean it's getting worse. <P>I had my Dad get as close as he could to hear it, but it's hard to detect where it's originating from because I have to be hitting a small bump rather quickly to receive the sound.<P>My dad says he notices it's exactley when the Wheel lefts at the peak of the bump, and it sounds like it's coming from inside the wheel.<P>Does this mean my shock is going bad?  What can I do to test if this is the problem?  Thanks in advance!<P>------------------<BR><B>It's sad, in the 20th Century, in the 1990's, we would have to still go the same bullshit route<BR>that artists have to go, to get acceptance.  If it wasn't for the independence, if it wasn't for the <BR>small little cities, and the few little ghetto guys, trying to make music, it never would have happened.<BR>Some of these guys will never make a dime, some of thse guys will be poor and die, alone.  <P>But in the proccess, they've been the true renegades.<P>And the true rebels always walk alone anyways.</B>||||reg||11
Z||000001||84Bill||05-01-2001||07:51 PM||||10 to 1 Its the brake pads flopping around. Hit the same bump with your foot lightly on the brake and listen no noise = pad retainer clips are either not installed or broken.||||reg||3
Z||000002||theogre||05-01-2001||07:56 PM||||What he said....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> inner rear brake pad is first thing to check.||||reg||1
